      "message": "fix(2d): ramp only at dead ends the plan marks; named fallback when too short\n\nReview of PR #3577, items 1, 3, 4 and 6.\n\n- Item 4: the dead end is now marked by the plan (`level_order::order`:\n  a later Outside pass that no lead-in reaches), not read from\n  `plunge_law::into_solid` at each pass link. The first entry of a level,\n  the ring 0 pieces and the Auto-order plan after a completeness-guard\n  fallback keep the entry of main; no earlier move is scanned again.\n- Item 1: a dead end too short for the ramp at the deepest descent of any\n  level sends the area to the Auto order with a note that carries\n  RINGS_FALLBACK (the StrategyFallback warning) and names the cause. A\n  ladder miss is named on the path.\n- Item 3: when the ramp stands in for a Plunge, Helix or Arc entry, the\n  path says so once, in the #2265 stand-in form.\n- Item 6: levels.rs no longer grows (459 on main, 456 now); the builders\n  move to the new module `level_ramp_entry.rs`.\n\nRefs #3567\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
