      "message": "test(2d): slope law and ramp pins for the dead-end entry\n\nReview of PR #3577, item 2. `late_entry_cut` counts a descending feed as\na ramp only at or under the ramp angle plus 0.05 deg and on the pass path;\na steeper feed counts like a plunge (`a_steep_straight_feed_is_not_a_ramp`).\nThe pin asserts that a ramp ran. New pins: the ramp angle, the floor under\nthe ramp, the width reading of the stepover band (it reads the band beside\nthe ring before, not a proof against a full-width cut), and the pure-Auto\nfallback of a dead end too short for the ramp. The grid helpers move to\n`pass_start_engagement/grid.rs` (400-line law).\n\nRefs #3567\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
